nment in  the energy environment context  and of course matters of corporate  sustainability and  brand new approaches radical new  approaches to environmental protection  he is a pioneer pioneering thinker in  helping us  reshape how we should think about  climate change and how to alleviate it  he is the author and editor or editor of  12 books and dozens of articles on  environmental protection regulatory  reform energy policy and sustainability  metrics  and their connections to corporate  strategy competitiveness so very much  rooted in the policy and the real world  he is he had a prize winning he's had  many prize-winning books uh his  latest book a 2019 book in which he has  edited a wonderful set of essays and i  would like to  highly recommend that i thoroughly  enjoyed reading it  and dan just mentioned that it's just  come out in paperback so i really urge  you all  to buy it and read it so this book was  just  awarded the financial ft book of the  year award and his previous prize  winning volume was green to gold  how smart companies use environmental  strategy to innovate creative create  value and build competitive advantage  and this has recently been named one of  the top green business books of the past  decade and he has had many interesting  articles i would like to point  one out that i think uh was particularly  impactful for me  red lights to green lights from 20th  century environmental regulation to 21st  century  sustainability so i wanted to say a  little bit about  his career trajectory only because of  how distinguished it is and how  varied it is and it gives you a sense of  someone who  really crosses disciplinary boundaries  that is a hallmark  of what we celebrate at the frankie  program from 2011 to 2014  uh professor st served as commissioner  of connecticut's department of energy  and environmental protection  where he earned a reputation for fresh  thinking and practical results  his policy innovations he launched many  policy i