 book  really has its place uh it is as you  heard uh  subtitled 40 big ideas for a sustainable  future  it is a a volume that uh i edited but  represents uh 56 different authors in  these 40 essays  offering up a range of perspectives from  a range of political starting points  and a range of underlying disciplines  including some folks who are  practitioners and not academics  but all offer interesting perspectives  on  critical issues and thoughtful carefully  constructed  analytically rigorous pathways forward  and that's what i'm actually very  excited to  dig into a bit today uh the book is by  the way  from yale university press a great  partnership with the long  time editor there who's done science and  environment gene thompson black  so really just a huge pleasure to have  been able to work with her  and to bring this volume to publication  in record time and it grows out of  an effort that the environment school by  the way those who have been following  you for a long time may not have  kept up with the fact that the yale  school of forestry and environmental  studies has rebranded itself as of a  couple of months ago  as the yale school of the environment  and the new dean of a few years ago indy  burke  launched the school on an effort to  rethink its direction and strategic plan  and one of the things that emerged was a  commitment to be more of a convening  platform  to bring people together to talk about  sustainability and how to get to a  sustainable future  and this book really grows out of that  broader dialogue the yale environmental  dialogue as we call it  organized by um uh dean indy burke and  now kind of a core part of the school's  program  and uh the book itself offers a a  range of concepts and principles for  thinking about environmental challenges  and related clean energy questions land  use issues natural resource management  so the full  spectrum of sustainability issues uh it  offers frameworks it looks at  technologies it looks 